<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> No, I want to see if people think it will work as an SCP and then develop it a bit more first</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Comedy, History??</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A viral Youtube video connecting a lot of the popular theories, things ranging from the Paul is dead theory, The Denver Airport, to the Black Knight Satellite, except this time the Foundation is thrown in and said to be the reason this all happened. The video has no anomalous properties, but it poses a threat to the secrecy of the Foundation.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The idea isn’t fully fleshed out yet, but what I am aiming for is it to tell a story about the Foundation that connects about four to five popular conspiracy theories, with neutralized SCP reports, breach reports, operation reports, and all of those mixed in. The theory will likely be super far-fetched, and the reports featured in the video are speculated to be fakes, which leads to the comedy at the end - When in the form of an addendum, one of the personnel hints at some, if not all of the theory being true.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> I think mainly the hook would be how the Foundation is connected to all of the theories, it’s going to be difficult but I want to write a lot of real-life events into it and explain it as an effect due to the Foundation.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The reason why this isn’t something like an incident report is that the video was never taken down, due to the fact that it went viral within twenty-four hours and the Foundation doesn’t have a way to track and supply amnestics to all the people who watched it. They conducted an operation that tries to influence the video to be viewed as a joke instead. Also, this may confuse some of you, so I’ll make it a bit clearer, but all the theories will be a chain of events, not a collection of events handled by the Foundation separately.</p>

