<p>The blending of 'ink blob that commits mass murder' and 'ink blob that inserts itself into text' feels&#8230;.weird here? Like the two things feel kinda&#8230;jarringly shoved together in a way that doesn't really blend together well for me. To be honest: both the mass murder and the text insertion are kinda&#8230;cliche at this point and I'm really not sure building on either will work unless you do something interesting with it, which brings me to my next thought.</p>
<p>There's not a lot of narrative meat to this; particularly since a lot of it seems to just be 'the scp keeps trying to escape' and like&#8230;that's a fine starting place for a story but the story has to end up going somewhere so this doesn't feel flat: something should change in regards to the escaping, whether it's the foundation figuring out a way to stop it, or the scp giving up, or the scp like, succeeding and escaping and doing something that means they can return to containment without the urge to escape again or something, y'know?</p>

