<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Article proceeds normally with several recovery logs detailing the circumstances surrounding particular subjects, most of which were only discovered after perpetrating acts of violence or suicide.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>When you say 'subjects' here, do you mean 'the SCP' or 'people affected by the SCP'?</p>
<p>My broader concerns with this are two fold. Firstly, it kinda feels like this is really blurring the lines between 'real' and 'not real' to a point where I don't really have a clear idea of how this works. Specifically, you mention people have a like 'uncanny valley' reaction to them that leads them to be ostracised; but you also have this thing where folk who meet them can end up assuming they've been friends for a long time and it kinda feels like there's this awkward mesh where they both can and can't infiltrate society?</p>
<p>Thematically, a lot of this reminds me of <a href="/scp-4857">SCP-4857</a> except it feels a lot blunter in it's questions.</p>
<p>My other big concern is that I'm not actually sure what this article will look like: the hook section indicates that there's meant to be this whole thing about being unsure if there's like, innocent people who have been arrested for crimes (and&#8230;I'm really not sure how that works: the implication of the infohazard is it only adds fake memories surrounding the SCP, not fake memories in general, and in turn, how can someone falsely remember murdering someone if they're still alive cos that implies they aren't an instance of the SCP?); but the additional notes imply this is meant to be much more about the effects of isolation in themes and I'm not sure how you're intending blending the two together.</p>
</div>
</div>
